{
  "conversation_lines": [
    {
      "turn_number": 1,
      "time": "2191-11-02 02:15:00",
      "speaker": "Doctor",
      "text": "Hi, I’m Dr. Lee. I’ll be part of your care team. You came in with high blood sugar and some symptoms—can you tell me what’s been going on?"
    },
    {
      "turn_number": 2,
      "time": "2191-11-02 02:17:00",
      "speaker": "Patient",
      "text": "Yes, for about three days my blood sugar has been over 300. I haven’t missed any insulin doses. I’ve also had this dry cough for weeks, and lately my eyes have been stinging and tearing."
    },
    {
      "turn_number": 3,
      "time": "2191-11-02 02:19:00",
      "speaker": "Doctor",
      "text": "I see. Any fevers, nausea, or pain when you urinate?"
    },
    {
      "turn_number": 4,
      "time": "2191-11-02 02:20:00",
      "speaker": "Patient",
      "text": "No fevers or nausea. And no, I don’t have any UTI symptoms this time, even though I’ve had them before. I did miss my weekly fosfomycin dose last week, though."
    },
    {
      "turn_number": 5,
      "time": "2191-11-02 02:22:00",
      "speaker": "Doctor",
      "text": "Okay. We also saw you were in mild diabetic ketoacidosis—your blood sugar was 406 and your acid levels were off. We’ve started you on IV fluids and insulin to correct that."
    },
    {
      "turn_number": 6,
      "time": "2191-11-02 02:24:00",
      "speaker": "Patient",
      "text": "Oh, that makes sense. I felt really weak and achy the day I came in. I knew something wasn’t right."
    },
    {
      "turn_number": 7,
      "time": "2191-11-02 02:26:00",
      "speaker": "Doctor",
      "text": "That’s common with DKA. We’re also checking your kidney function. Your creatinine was elevated at 1.9, which suggests some acute kidney injury, but it’s likely due to dehydration from high sugars."
    },
    {
      "turn_number": 8,
      "time": "2191-11-02 02:28:00",
      "speaker": "Patient",
      "text": "I haven’t been eating much. My mom’s been in the hospital, and I’ve been stressed about my son too. I just haven’t had an appetite."
    },
    {
      "turn_number": 9,
      "time": "2191-11-02 02:30:00",
      "speaker": "Doctor",
      "text": "That stress and poor intake can definitely affect your blood sugar control. We’ll help you stabilize that. Your transplant team also checked your cyclosporine level—it was a bit low at 47, but we’ll keep monitoring it."
    },
    {
      "turn_number": 10,
      "time": "2191-11-02 02:32:00",
      "speaker": "Patient",
      "text": "I take it exactly as prescribed. Is that level concerning?"
    },
    {
      "turn_number": 11,
      "time": "2191-11-02 02:34:00",
      "speaker": "Doctor",
      "text": "It’s slightly below the ideal range, but not dangerous. We’ll keep an eye on it. You’re still on your full immunosuppression—Cellcept, cyclosporine, and prednisone—all unchanged."
    },
    {
      "turn_number": 12,
      "time": "2191-11-02 02:36:00",
      "speaker": "Patient",
      "text": "Good. I don’t want any issues with my transplant."
    },
    {
      "turn_number": 13,
      "time": "2191-11-02 02:38:00",
      "speaker": "Doctor",
      "text": "We’re not seeing any signs of rejection. Your renal ultrasound was normal—no blockage or swelling in the kidney. Resistive indices actually improved a bit."
    },
    {
      "turn_number": 14,
      "time": "2191-11-02 02:40:00",
      "speaker": "Patient",
      "text": "That’s a relief. What about my cough? My PCP thought it might be allergies from my car’s AC filter."
    },
    {
      "turn_number": 15,
      "time": "2191-11-02 02:42:00",
      "speaker": "Doctor",
      "text": "We did a CT scan of your chest today. It shows stable changes from your past radiation—no signs of infection, pneumonia, or new lung issues. Your cough is likely due to allergies or postnasal drip."
    },
    {
      "turn_number": 16,
      "time": "2191-11-02 02:44:00",
      "speaker": "Patient",
      "text": "So not an infection?"
    },
    {
      "turn_number": 17,
      "time": "2191-11-02 02:46:00",
      "speaker": "Doctor",
      "text": "No. Your white blood cell count is normal, and we tested for viruses, Legionella, and BK virus—all negative. So it’s not a viral or bacterial infection."
    },
    {
      "turn_number": 18,
      "time": "2191-11-02 02:48:00",
      "speaker": "Patient",
      "text": "Okay, that’s good. But my eyes still feel irritated."
    },
    {
      "turn_number": 19,
      "time": "2191-11-02 02:50:00",
      "speaker": "Doctor",
      "text": "That could be related to the same allergies. We’re going to start you on a nasal spray—Nasacort—to help with the postnasal drip and eye symptoms."
    },
    {
      "turn_number": 20,
      "time": "2191-11-02 02:52:00",
      "speaker": "Patient",
      "text": "I was supposed to start fluticasone, but I never picked it up."
    },
    {
      "turn_number": 21,
      "time": "2191-11-02 02:54:00",
      "speaker": "Doctor",
      "text": "Nasacort is similar and should help. We’ll send it home with you—use two sprays in each nostril once daily."
    },
    {
      "turn_number": 22,
      "time": "2191-11-02 08:15:00",
      "speaker": "Doctor",
      "text": "Good morning. Your blood sugar is coming down—now 186—and your acid levels are improving. We’re transitioning you back to your insulin pump."
    },
    {
      "turn_number": 23,
      "time": "2191-11-02 08:17:00",
      "speaker": "Patient",
      "text": "Great. Will the pump settings stay the same?"
    },
    {
      "turn_number": 24,
      "time": "2191-11-02 08:19:00",
      "speaker": "Doctor",
      "text": "The endocrine team adjusted your basal rates slightly to help prevent future highs. For example, your morning rate is now a bit higher to cover dawn phenomenon."
    },
    {
      "turn_number": 25,
      "time": "2191-11-02 08:21:00",
      "speaker": "Patient",
      "text": "Okay, I can update that. What about my kidney numbers?"
    },
    {
      "turn_number": 26,
      "time": "2191-11-02 08:23:00",
      "speaker": "Doctor",
      "text": "Your creatinine dropped to 1.6—much better. It’s responding well to fluids. We expect it to keep improving."
    },
    {
      "turn_number": 27,
      "time": "2191-11-03 09:00:00",
      "speaker": "Doctor",
      "text": "Your labs this morning look good. Glucose is 93, bicarbonate is normal, and creatinine is now 1.1. Your DKA has resolved."
    },
    {
      "turn_number": 28,
      "time": "2191-11-03 09:02:00",
      "speaker": "Patient",
      "text": "That’s a big improvement. Does that mean I can go home soon?"
    },
    {
      "turn_number": 29,
      "time": "2191-11-03 09:04:00",
      "speaker": "Doctor",
      "text": "Yes, likely tomorrow. Your cough and eye symptoms aren’t from infection, so we’re confident it’s safe to discharge you with the nasal spray."
    },
    {
      "turn_number": 30,
      "time": "2191-11-03 09:06:00",
      "speaker": "Patient",
      "text": "And my transplant is okay?"
    },
    {
      "turn_number": 31,
      "time": "2191-11-03 09:08:00",
      "speaker": "Doctor",
      "text": "Yes. Your cyclosporine level this morning was 52—solidly in the target range. Keep taking all your immunosuppressants and Bactrim as prescribed."
    },
    {
      "turn_number": 32,
      "time": "2191-11-03 09:10:00",
      "speaker": "Patient",
      "text": "I will. Should I restart my weekly fosfomycin?"
    },
    {
      "turn_number": 33,
      "time": "2191-11-03 09:12:00",
      "speaker": "Doctor",
      "text": "Yes, continue it as before. It’s helping prevent UTIs, especially with your history and immunosuppression."
    },
    {
      "turn_number": 34,
      "time": "2191-11-03 14:00:00",
      "speaker": "Doctor",
      "text": "We’re finalizing your discharge plan. You’ll go home tomorrow. We just need to make sure you’re stable overnight."
    },
    {
      "turn_number": 35,
      "time": "2191-11-03 14:02:00",
      "speaker": "Patient",
      "text": "What about follow-up?"
    },
    {
      "turn_number": 36,
      "time": "2191-11-03 14:04:00",
      "speaker": "Doctor",
      "text": "You’ll need blood work in a few days—sodium, potassium, creatinine, and glucose. We’ll fax the order to your local lab. Also, follow up with your primary doctor and endocrinologist."
    },
    {
      "turn_number": 37,
      "time": "2191-11-03 14:06:00",
      "speaker": "Patient",
      "text": "And the pending tests—BK virus, strep antigen?"
    },
    {
      "turn_number": 38,
      "time": "2191-11-03 14:08:00",
      "speaker": "Doctor",
      "text": "Those are still pending, but given your symptoms and clear CT, it’s unlikely they’ll change anything. Your doctor will review them at your follow-up."
    },
    {
      "turn_number": 39,
      "time": "2191-11-04 10:30:00",
      "speaker": "Doctor",
      "text": "You’re doing well. Vital signs are stable, and you’ve been eating and drinking without issue. We’re clearing you for discharge."
    },
    {
      "turn_number": 40,
      "time": "2191-11-04 10:32:00",
      "speaker": "Patient",
      "text": "Thank you. I feel much better."
    },
    {
      "turn_number": 41,
      "time": "2191-11-04 10:34:00",
      "speaker": "Doctor",
      "text": "You’re welcome. Keep using the Nasacort daily, monitor your blood sugar closely, and take all your medications. Call your doctor if you develop fever, shortness of breath, or high sugars again."
    },
    {
      "turn_number": 42,
      "time": "2191-11-04 10:36:00",
      "speaker": "Patient",
      "text": "I will. And I’ll get that lab work done."
    },
    {
      "turn_number": 43,
      "time": "2191-11-04 10:38:00",
      "speaker": "Doctor",
      "text": "Perfect. Take care, and we’ll see you in follow-up if needed."
    },
    {
      "turn_number": 44,
      "time": "2191-11-04 10:40:00",
      "speaker": "Patient",
      "text": "Thank you, Dr. Lee."
    }
  ],
  "summary": {
    "admission_start": "2191-11-02 01:54:00",
    "admission_end": "2191-11-04 17:30:00",
    "summary_paragraph": "A woman with a history of type 1 diabetes, kidney transplant, and recurrent UTIs was admitted for hyperglycemia and a persistent dry cough. She was found to be in mild diabetic ketoacidosis with a blood glucose of 406 and an anion gap of 16, along with acute kidney injury (creatinine 1.9). She was treated with IV fluids and an insulin drip, then transitioned back to her insulin pump with adjusted basal rates. Her kidney function improved (creatinine 1.1) and DKA resolved. Evaluation for infection included a negative CT chest for pneumonia, negative respiratory viral panel, and negative urine Legionella antigen. Her chronic cough and eye discomfort were attributed to allergic rhinitis, likely triggered by environmental factors, and she was started on Nasacort nasal spray. She remained on her baseline immunosuppressive and chronic medications, with stable cyclosporine levels. She was discharged home in stable condition with follow-up labs and primary care appointments.",
    "problems": [
      "Type 1 diabetes mellitus with ketoacidosis without coma",
      "Acute kidney failure, unspecified",
      "Other complication of kidney transplant",
      "Allergic rhinitis, unspecified",
      "Long term (current) use of insulin",
      "Presence of insulin pump (external) (internal)",
      "Type 1 diabetes mellitus with diabetic nephropathy",
      "Essential (primary) hypertension",
      "Hypothyroidism, unspecified",
      "Personal history of malignant neoplasm of breast"
    ]
  }
}
